{"search_result_groups":[{"search_result_type":"webResults","items":[{"index":null,"title":"Routes · Undertale | Game Design Lab","snippets":["Routes · Undertale | Game Design Lab Undertale / Game design / Routes Full-game spoilers. This research discusses encounters, characters and endings. Return to Overview Look up the reference 06 Routes Contents Routes Every playthrough resolves to exactly one of three routes, tabled in full in the routes and endings reference. Which one a save gets is decided by two systems the player metrics section keeps separate (the visible EXP/LV pair, and the per-region kill counters and hidden Murder Level that gate Genocide specifically) so a run can carry a high LV from killing without having met a single Genocide requirement. True Pacifist Gated behind a completed Neutral ending, so it cannot be reached on a first playthrough. Its requirement is zero EXP for the entire run (not merely \"spare everything,\" since any kill anywhere disqualifies it) plus the eleven-step friendship chain: Toriel spared, Papyrus's date completed, Undyne's cooking lesson, Mettaton EX talked down by rating rather than fought, and Alphys's letter leading to the True Lab and ... a permanent flag: Chara's ERASE/DO NOT choice both lead to the same reset, and accepting Chara's offer to restore the world alters every subsequent True Pacifist and Genocide ending on that save, detailed in the reference's soulless-routes table. Waterfall's text gate on the path to the bridge: it fires only while the region's kill counter is still short, one of the route's few explicit warnings before an early approach permanently aborts it. A run can also fall short of Genocide without reverting cleanly to a default Neutral ending: aborting partway leaves the kill counters and Murder Level exactly where they stopped, and the Alphys ending exists specifically to catch a Genocide attempt abandoned in Hotland. The full flag ladder behind these routing decisions (Murder Level's 18 save-